ReplayKit patch 3 of 4 for win-capture-audio 2.3.4 (Ayrton09, commit d11b381).

A program that dies while it is captured can make the audio service take the capture buffer away in the middle of a
read. The copy of the packet out of that buffer (Mixer::SubmitPacket) then faults inside the capture thread, an access
violation that nothing in the plugin catches, and obs goes down with it: the crash report of 2026-10-06 shows exactly
that, memmove under SubmitPacket under ForwardPacket, in the capture thread of the plugin. The copy is now made behind a
handler that takes only a fault inside the buffer being read (any other fault, in memory that is not the engine buffer,
stays the crash it is, so real memory damage is never hidden), a packet that could not be read ends the capture so it
starts over on a fresh client, a success code that carries no buffer is no longer read as a packet, and no exception of
any kind can leave the capture thread or the worker of the mixer.

